      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town’s name combines the English word \"dale\" for valley with \"lawn,\" describing its grassy valley setting.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        28
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.theroute-66.com/lawndale.html",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "A sawmill built by early settler Thomas Esten on Kickapoo Creek marked the first industry in what would become Lawndale.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.theroute-66.com/lawndale.html",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Lawndale sits on Historic Route 66, a famed stretch of highway that once connected Chicago to Los Angeles.",
